# leakguard patterns — one case-insensitive literal per line, # for comments.
#
# THIS FILE IS AN EXAMPLE AND IS COMMITTED. Your real list is copied to
# .git/leakguard-patterns, which lives inside .git and is therefore never
# pushed — a denylist of secret names committed to a public repo publishes
# exactly what it is meant to protect.
#
# Put here the things that must never reach a public commit:
#
# Client names and abbreviations
# AcmeCorp
# ACME
#
# Private repo and project names
# my-private-tool
# internal-dashboard
#
# Internal hosts, orgs and domains
# vpn.internal.example
# my-github-org
#
# Built-in checks need no configuration: absolute /home/<user> and /Users/<user>
# paths, email addresses (github noreply and example.com excepted), and private
# key headers.
